From 599e3eb195109c5377ba858aa7031c4a67617c0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Reilly <jreilly1821@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 07:34:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Media over the mesh, with a size cap
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A content repository small enough for a BLE hop.

- `POST /_matrix/media/v3/upload` stores the body verbatim under
  `mxc://{our name}/{id}`; `GET /_matrix/client/v1/media/download` (the
  authenticated path) and its legacy `/_matrix/media/v3/download` twin
  serve it with the spec's inline-or-attachment disposition and CSP.
- `GET /_matrix/media/v3/config` and `/_matrix/client/v1/media/config`
  advertise `m.upload.size`, the cap: 256 KiB by default,
  `NEUTRINO_MEDIA_MAX_BYTES` overrides. An upload over it is refused
  `413 M_TOO_LARGE` on its declared length before the body is read, and
  capped as it is read when nothing is declared.
- `GET /_matrix/federation/v1/media/download/{id}` serves what this
  server's users uploaded to an authenticated peer as `multipart/mixed`
  (metadata part, then content), the spec's shape. A download for
  another server's `mxc://` that this node does not hold is fetched from
  that server once, refused unread over the cap, cached under the
  peer's name, and served — so a photo sent on one phone opens on the
  next.
- Blobs live in the store (`media` table): uploads are capped small,
  and one file to back up beats a second store on disk.

Complement: TestMediaConfig joins the allowlist.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
